<text>if (!ocelot_can_inject(ocelot, 0))</text>
<text>ocelot_port_inject_frame(ocelot, port, 0, rew_op, skb);</text>
Reason:
Both `ocelot_can_inject()` and `ocelot_port_inject_frame()` contain `lockdep_assert_held()` for the injection group lock, but `ocelot_port_xmit_inj()` called them without first acquiring that lock (via `ocelot_lock_inj_grp()`). This missing lock protection can lead to race conditions with other callers concurrently accessing injection registers, causing data corruption or lockdep warnings.

