`ocelot_lock_inj_grp()` is added before the `ocelot_can_inject()` check to acquire the injection group lock, and `ocelot_unlock_inj_grp()` is added after the frame is injected (and also on the error paths) to release the lock. This ensures serialized access to the injection registers, matching the locking pattern used by the correct caller `felix_port_deferred_xmit()`.


